GET https://datamall2.mytransport.sg/ltaodataservice/v3/BusArrival?BusStopCode=04121 Header: AccountKey: [your key from the email] # BusStopCode is the only required parameter. # Add &ServiceNo=7 to ask about one service only. # Refreshes every 20 seconds. JSON comes back by default. Copy Check your key once, from Terminal (Mac) or PowerShell (Windows) Type read -s LTA_KEY on a Mac, or $k = Read-Host "Paste LTA key" on Windows, and press Return . Paste your key and press Return . On a Mac nothing appears, and that is expected. Click Copy on the line for your machine, the first for a Mac and the second for Windows, paste it and press Return . Read the last line. HTTP status: 200 means your key works. curl -sS -w "
HTTP status: %{http_code}
" -H "AccountKey: $LTA_KEY" "https://datamall2.mytransport.sg/ltaodataservice/v3/BusArrival?BusStopCode=04121" Copy curl.exe -sS -w "
HTTP status: %{http_code}
" -H "AccountKey: $k" "https://datamall2.mytransport.sg/ltaodataservice/v3/BusArrival?BusStopCode=04121" Copy The Windows line says curl.exe because in Windows PowerShell plain curl is a different command. The address bar cannot send the header, so it always answers 404. Section VII repeats this when you need the JSON for the master prompt. Stops around this building Code Description Road 04121 SMU —the default Stamford Rd 04179 Aft Bras Basah Stn Exit A Bras Basah Rd 01012 Hotel Grand Pacific Victoria St 04151 Cath of The Good Shepherd Victoria St 04159 Aft CHIJMES Victoria St 08069 Bencoolen Stn Exit B Bras Basah Rd Use 04121. It is seventy metres from the School of Accountancy and seventy-three from SMU Connexion, so you can stand at the physical stop and compare it with your own screen. Around thirty services call there, but many run only at peak hours, so the board shows fewer in the afternoon. Two version traps. Bus Arrival has been v3 since August 2024. The old BusArrivalv2 path from older tutorials now returns 404 The requested API was not found , exactly like a missing key, so a pasted old URL looks like a key problem. The ERP Rates API was removed on 30 September 2024, so a guide that still describes it is out of date elsewhere too. The leading zero is part of the code A stop code is five digits , and community websites strip the leading zero: one popular site displays our stop as "B/S 4121". The code you type is 04121. If your screen is empty and your key is right, count the digits before you blame anything else. Building Autonomous AI Agents &middot; Day 1 &middot; Full End-to-End Build Prof. Sungjong Roh, PhD &middot; SMU &middot; Lee Kong Chian School of Business The error that will cost you an hour, and the one that saves it Different failures, different codes Almost every service answers a missing credential with 401 , which says plainly what is wrong. LTA does not, and its exact behaviour hands you a free diagnostic. These are real responses, checked live on 24 September 2026. What you sent Code Body No AccountKey header at all 404 The requested API was not found Header with an empty value, e.g. code that falls back to '' 404 the same as no header Header present, wrong key 401 nothing at all, an empty body Variable never set , so your code sends the word undefined 401 identical to a wrong key , which is the trap below Mis-cased path, or the old BusArrivalv2 404 the same as a missing key BusStopCode missing or wrongly capitalised 403 an HTML Access Denied page Why the shaded row matters most. If your Vercel variable was never saved, or was saved and never redeployed, then process.env.LTA_ACCOUNT_KEY is undefined . JavaScript does not drop that header: it sends the nine-letter word undefined , and LTA answers 401 , byte for byte the same as a genuinely wrong key. So the commonest failure of the afternoon and the one everybody guesses first look identical from the outside , which is why the function has to say which it was. Read the code, then act 404 The header never arrived, arrived empty, or the path is wrong. Check, in this order: is the header spelled AccountKey , one word, because accountkey is fine but Account-Key is a different header; does it carry a value at all; is the path spelled with the documentation's capitals, because /v3/Busarrival is a 404 even with a correct key. Plain http is not a cause: LTA redirects it to https and fetch follows. 401 Some value arrived and LTA refused it. Two different faults land here and you cannot tell them apart from the outside, so read /api/health first . If keyConfigured is false, the variable is missing or you never redeployed. If it is true, the value itself is wrong, so re-copy it from the email and watch for a trailing space. 403 An Access Denied page means the stop code never arrived. The parameter must be spelled BusStopCode exactly, with those capitals. Getting a 401 after a string of 404s is still progress : the address and the header name are now right, and the whole chain from your page to your function to LTA is connected. What remains is the value, and keyConfigured tells you whether the value is wrong or simply absent. Principle An error message is a claim the system makes about itself, and systems are often unhelpful about their own failures. Learn what your service does when it is unhappy , because the textbook meaning of a code is not always the local one. Building Autonomous AI Agents &middot; Day 1 &middot; Full End-to-End Build Prof. Sungjong Roh, PhD &middot; SMU &middot; Lee Kong Chian School of Business IV &middot; What a key actually is, and why anyone would want yours An API key is not quite a password. A password proves you are you, so that a service can show you your own things. A key is closer to a name badge worn by your software: it tells the provider which caller this is, so they can count the calls, apply the limits, and switch you off if you misbehave.

